{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"flowered-nonvalued-mink","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\nIn `sweep (windows)` diag run 44591481319 (throwaway branch `w1-diag-opcert-acl`, carrying the plump-smelly-indianabat and undamaging-ashamed-wasp fixes), `tests/unit/test_opcert_key_copy_leak_tortoise.py::test_signer_test_modules_leave_no_key_copy_in_the_temp_dir` failed. Its nested pytest run of `test_opcert_service.py` + `test_opcert_service_integrity.py` reported 7 failed, 9 passed. One failure is `git commit failed ... open(\"<id>/<event>-CREATE.json\"): Filename too long`. The others are jobs ending with `status: error`. In the same run, the same tests run outside the nesting all pass.\n\n## Cause (hypothesis, tested by the change)\nThe test roots the nested run's TMPDIR sandbox (`tmp_path/tmpdir-sandbox`) and its basetemp (`tmp_path/run/nested-pytest`) under its own `tmp_path`. On the runner that is `C:\\Users\\runneradmin\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\pytest-of-runneradmin\\pytest-0\\popen-gw0\\test_signer_test_modules_leave0\\`. Job workspaces (`rebar-opcert-ws-*\\.tickets-tracker\\<id>\\<long event name>.json`) and ticket stores under that prefix pass Windows' 260-character MAX_PATH, and git is not built with `core.longpaths`.\n\n## Approach\nTest-only change. A new fixture `short_root` creates `tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"tort-\")` directly under the system temp dir, so the root is short, private and unique per test. The test uses `short_root/\"t\"` as the TMPDIR sandbox and `short_root/\"r\"` as the nested basetemp root. The fixture removes the root in a `finally`. The leak assertion (no `rebar-opcert-*` left in the sandbox) is unchanged. No product code, config key, env var or flag changes. Portable: uses `tempfile` and `pathlib` only.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_key_copy_leak_tortoise.py` — the fixture and the test's two paths.\n\n## Testing\n- The test itself passes on macOS/Linux (`make verify`), and on Windows in a pre-merge diag run on the throwaway branch.\n- After merge: it passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `test_signer_test_modules_leave_no_key_copy_in_the_temp_dir` roots its nested TMPDIR and basetemp in a short private temp dir that it removes afterwards, and still asserts no key copy is left behind.\n- [ ] The test passes in a `sweep (windows)` run on main.","id":"d4f1-da58-0748-4e1a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["windows","portability","tests"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows: the nested signer-module leak test exceeds MAX_PATH (\"Filename too long\") under its tmp_path sandbox"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1795114377192718375,"uuid":"9d57f178-a965-4e11-8076-33e9e6de1d4f"}